      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LUCKY CHANCE (2) goes on top. He was a very good winner at Coleraine in a strong race two back beating Raise The Note which is good form for this. He's since had a tickover flat run in a maiden (which he still is, on the flat) but he looks nicely placed here. BAZINI (1) has struggled his past couple of runs but was a nice winner three back at Warrnambool and his best is good enough. CHARLIE MESSY HAIR (3) was a good winner here two back before a nice tickover run back on the flat. He should take some beating. NIGHTFALL (5) has just been fair in two Australian runs but wasn't bad here two back and is in the mix from CHRISTMAS (4) who is improving.",
